    {
      "heading": "How Czech grammar works",
      "text": [
        "Czech shows a word's job in the sentence with endings rather than word order. Nouns, adjectives and pronouns change their ending for 7 cases, 2 numbers (singular, plural) and 3 genders, and verbs change their ending for person and number.",
        "This guide covers the patterns that handle most everyday words. Learn the case meanings first, then one noun pattern per gender — every other table here follows the same layout. Czech textbooks and dictionaries number the cases 1–7 (1. pád, 2. pád, …), so the numbers are shown too."
      ]
